participating-org.narrative:
The purpose of ASA is to support communities in finding sustainable solutions to their social problems, focusing on the areas of agriculture, water and sanitation, education, health, advocacy and communication, and spirituality.  The objectives of ASA are to:
a) Stimulate the integral development of communities;
b) Promote the sustainable development of communities, in cooperation with other similar and/or religious and humanitarian institutions;
c) Encourage the strengthening of the organizational and institutional capacity of communities, with a view to the self-satisfaction of their basic needs and the development of a participatory community life;
d) Promote actions that contribute to human development, as well as to harmony and dignity among people.                                                                                                                                               ASA's MISSION is to Promote the pursuit of peace and sustainable solutions that contribute to holistic development aimed at the well-being of the human being and the preservation of God's creation..

ASA's VISION  communities with integral and abundant life.
